{{Dependencies|Module:LuaInfobox|Module:Arguments|Module:ACandy}}
This template implements a simple interface to construct an infobox. It can either be used to create an infobox directly on a content page or to create an infobox template.

{{clear}}
==Basic usage ==
{{LuaInfobox
| title = Miraheze
| image = Miraheze Logo.svg
| image-size = 150px
| caption = Honeycomb logo of Miraheze
| -header :: Basic info
| Founded :: 2015
| Operator :: Wikitide Foundation
| -header :: Statistics
| Number of wikis :: {{NUMBEROFWIKIS}}
| Number of active wikis :: {{NUMBEROFACTIVEWIKIS}}
| :: Some arbitrary text. You can even put a <div style{{=}}"color: red">div</div> here.
}}

Unlike other infoboxes, the labels and data are separated by <code>::</code> instead of <code>=</code>. These parameters are presented in the infobox in order.

<syntaxhighlight lang=wikitext>
{{LuaInfobox
| title = Miraheze
| image = Miraheze Logo.svg
| image-size = 150px
| caption = Honeycomb logo of Miraheze

| -header :: Basic info
| Founded :: 2015
| Operator :: Wikitide Foundation

| -header :: Statistics
| Number of wikis :: {{NUMBEROFWIKIS}}
| Number of active wikis :: {{NUMBEROFACTIVEWIKIS}}
| :: Some arbitrary text. You can even put a <div style{{=}}"color: red">div</div> here.
}}
</syntaxhighlight>

==Customizing the infobox==
This infobox can be customized in several ways. 

The <code>class</code> argument adds a class to the infobox, and a custom stylesheet can modify it. It is also possible to add inline styles to this infobox. See the list of possible parameters for more information.

==Tabbing==
===Prerequisite===
{{GadgetInstructions|name=Tab}}<!-- 
Empty template used for adding a category that loads the Tab gadget
-->
{{Tab}}
===Simple tabbing===
{{LuaInfobox
|title = Shiroko
|-tabs :: Variant 1 :: Variant 2

|Name :: Shiroko

|-tab-start :: 1
|Age :: 17
|Hobby :: Cycling

|-tab-start :: 2
|Age :: 21
|Hobby :: Jogging
|-tab-end :: 2

|Affiliation :: Abydos
}}
The wikitext below creates a simple infobox with tabs. Argument <code>-tabs :: tab name 1 :: tab name 2 :: ...</code> creates buttons, while <code>-tab-start :: 1</code> specifies the beginning of the content for tab 1. Note that <code>-tab-end</code> is optional if it is immediately followed by the start of another tab or the end of the template.
<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext">
{{LuaInfobox
|title = Shiroko
|-tabs :: Variant 1 :: Variant 2

|Name :: Shiroko

<!-- Content for variant 1-->
|-tab-start :: 1
|Age :: 17
|Hobby :: Cycling

<!-- Content for variant 2-->
|-tab-start :: 2
|Age :: 21
|Hobby :: Jogging
|-tab-end :: 2

<!-- This is shared between both tabs -->
|Affiliation :: Abydos
}}
</syntaxhighlight>

===Advanced tabbing===
{{LuaInfobox
|title=Shiroko
|-tabs :: Variant 1 :: Variant 2

|Name :: Shiroko

|-tab-start :: 1
|Age :: 17
|Hobby :: Cycling

|-tab-start :: 2
|Age :: 21
|-header :: Special abilities
|Ability 1 :: Drone attack
|Ability 2 :: Self-buff
|-tab-end :: 2

|-header :: Other information
|Affiliation :: Abydos
|Club :: Foreclosure Task Force

|-tab-start :: 1
|Friend(s) :: Hoshino
}}
Below is an advanced example. Note that:
# Tab content can contain extra rows. For example, variant 2 not only has extra rows ("Ability 1" and "Ability 2") but also an extra header ("Special abilities").
# Tab content does not need to be continuous. For example, variant 1's content is present both at the beginning and the end of the infobox.

<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext" copy>
{{LuaInfobox
|title=Shiroko
|-tabs :: Variant 1 :: Variant 2

|Name :: Shiroko

|-tab-start :: 1
|Age :: 17
|Hobby :: Cycling

|-tab-start :: 2
|Age :: 21
|-header :: Special abilities
|Ability 1 :: Drone attack
|Ability 2 :: Self-buff
|-tab-end :: 2

|-header :: Other information
|Affiliation :: Abydos
|Club :: Foreclosure Task Force

|-tab-start :: 1
|Friend(s) :: Hoshino
}}
</syntaxhighlight>

==Using it as the basis of other infoboxes==
This template is intended to be used as a basis for other infoboxes. Suppose we have an infobox for a person, we could write it as follows. Note how we are able to apply arbitrary templates before sending data to the infobox. This provides us flexibility while the implementation remains simple.

If we want to skip a row when data is missing, the parameter can be left empty. The <code>office</code> parameter below gives an example.
<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext" copy>
<includeonly>{{LuaInfobox
| title = {{{name|}}}
| -header :: Basic info
| Name :: {{{name|}}}
| Birthday :: {{{birthday|}}}
| Age :: {{ Calculate age | {{{birthday|}}} }}
| -header :: Career
| Institution :: [[{{{institution|}}}]]
| {{ #if: {{{office|}}} | Office :: {{{office|}}} | }}
}}</includeonly>
</syntaxhighlight>

